\lispPackageChapter{chorus/api/defkernel}

This package defines kernels and launches them. \texttt{chorus/api} reexports
it. It does not reexport \texttt{chorus/api/kernel-manager}. A kernel defined
here is registered on \texttt{*kernel-manager*} and compiled the first time it
is launched.

\lispMacroSubsection{defkernel}

\lispSyntax

\texttt{(defkernel \lispVar{name} (\lispVar{return-type} \lispVar{arguments})
  \&body \lispVar{body})}

Each argument has the form \texttt{(\lispVar{var} \lispVar{type})}. The macro
defines a Lisp function of those variables with keyword arguments
\texttt{grid-dim} and \texttt{block-dim}. Both default to \texttt{(1 1 1)}.
The launch uses \texttt{cu-launch-kernel} and the stream in
\texttt{chorus/api/context:*cuda-stream*}.

\lispMacroSubsection{defkernelmacro}

\lispSyntax

\texttt{(defkernelmacro \lispVar{name} \lispVar{arguments} \&body \lispVar{body})}

Defines a macro in the kernel language.

\lispMacroSubsection{defkernel-symbol-macro}

\lispSyntax

\texttt{(defkernel-symbol-macro \lispVar{name} \lispVar{expansion})}

Defines a symbol macro in the kernel language.

\lispMacroSubsection{defglobal}

\lispSyntax

\texttt{(defglobal \lispVar{name} \lispVar{expression} \&optional \lispVar{qualifiers})}

Defines a kernel global. When \texttt{qualifiers} is omitted, the qualifier is
\texttt{:device}.

\lispFunctionSubsection{global-ref}

Returns the device pointer of a global after ensuring it is loaded.

\lispFunctionSubsection{expand-macro-1}

Expands one kernel-macro call.

\lispFunctionSubsection{expand-macro}

Expands kernel macros in a form.

\section{The kernel manager}

\texttt{chorus/api/kernel-manager} holds the definitions and the loaded CUDA
module. \texttt{*kernel-manager*} is that object. \texttt{defkernel} calls
\texttt{kernel-manager-define-function}. A launch calls
\texttt{ensure-kernel-function-loaded}. \texttt{with-cuda} calls
\texttt{kernel-manager-unload} when the context ends.

The package also exports \texttt{make-kernel-manager}, the
\texttt{kernel-manager-*} readers, \texttt{kernel-manager-compile-module},
\texttt{kernel-manager-load-module}, \texttt{kernel-manager-load-function},
\texttt{kernel-manager-load-global}, and the other \texttt{ensure-kernel-*}
operations.
